//! Per-constellation ACR (Acquisition Correlation Ratio) lookup tables
//! mapping r_A = (V^m / V^s)² → C/N0 (dB-Hz).
//!
//! Generated by Monte Carlo simulation of the production acquisition
//! functions (`examples/gen_acr_tables.rs`) on the real data path: the
//! TART sampling rate (16.368 MHz, 16 samples per chip) with one-bit
//! quantization (`simulator::quantize_bipolar_demean`), exactly as the
//! acquisition pipeline consumes an `Observation`.  A table calibrated on
//! unquantized signals underestimates C/N0 by ~2-3 dB on one-bit data,
//! because the recovered coherent amplitude drops by sqrt(2/π) in the
//! weak-signal limit.
//!
//! Each table is computed for the coherent integration time actually used
//! by the acquisition (two code periods) and the constellation's own code
//! sidelobe structure, so a table is only valid for the constellation(s)
//! named in its documentation.

